          "number": 3,
          "letter": "C",
          "english": "Today we can no longer ignore the ecological curses that we have released in our search for warmth and comfort. In engineering and exploiting and transforming our habitat, we have opened tens of thousands of Pandora's boxes. In recent decades, environmental threats have expanded beyond regional boundaries to have global reach and, most hauntingly, are multiplying at a dizzying rate. On a regular basis, we are reminded that we are running out of time. Year after year, faster and faster, consumption outpaces the biological capacity of our planet. Stories of accelerated catastrophe multiply. We fear the breakdown of the electric grid, the end of non-renewable resources, the expansion of deserts, the loss of islands, and the pollution of our air and water.",
          "chinese": "如今，我们再也不能忽视那些为了寻求温暖与舒适而释放出的生态诅咒。在改造、开发和改变我们的栖息地的过程中，我们打开了数以万计的潘多拉魔盒。近几十年来，环境威胁已经超越地区边界，扩展到全球范围；最令人不安的是，这些威胁正以令人眩晕的速度不断增加。我们经常被提醒，我们的时间所剩无几。年复一年，速度越来越快，消费的增长超过了地球的生物承载能力。关于灾难加速的故事越来越多。我们担心电网崩溃、不可再生资源耗尽、沙漠扩张、岛屿消失，以及空气和水受到污染。",
