          "english": "Should you find yourself on the receiving end of this kind of complaining, there's an ingenious way to shut it down—which is to agree with it, ardently. Psychotherapist Lori Gottlieb describes this as \"over-validation\". For one thing, you'll be spared further moaning, since the other person's motivation was to confirm her beliefs, and now you're confirming them. But for another, as Gottlieb notes, people confronted with over-validation often hear their complaints afresh and start arguing back. The notion that they're utterly powerless suddenly seems unrealistic—not to mention rather annoying—so they're prompted instead to generate ideas about how they might change things.",
          "chinese": "如果你发现自己成为了这种抱怨的承受对象，有一个绝妙的方法可以终止它——那就是热烈地赞同它。心理治疗师洛里·戈特利布（Lori Gottlieb）将此描述为“过度认可”。一方面，你将无需再听进一步的抱怨，因为对方的动机本就是为了证实她的信念，而你现在正在证实它们。但另一方面，正如戈特利布所指出的，面临过度认可的人往往会重新倾听自己的抱怨并开始反驳。认为自己彻底无能为力的想法突然显得很不现实——更不用说还相当令人厌烦——因此他们反而会被促使去构想他们可以如何改变现状的设想。",
